          "9702_formula_hookes_law"
        ]
      },
      "hints": [
        "The spring constant is the gradient of the force–extension relationship, so find the extension rather than using the spring length directly.",
        "At 12.0 N, the graph gives a length of 24 cm; subtract the zero-force length of 8 cm and convert the extension to metres."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Hooke's law gives F = kx, so k = F / x; equivalently, k is the gradient of the force–extension graph.",
        "At zero force the spring length is 8 cm. At 12.0 N its length is 24 cm, so the extension is 24 − 8 = 16 cm = 0.160 m.",
        "Thus k = 12.0 / 0.160 = 75 N m⁻¹."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "deterministic_checks": [],
        "full_marks_if_all_deterministic_checks_pass": false,
        "ai_rubric": [
          {
            "criterion_id": "9702_s23_22_q04_b_mp01",
            "observable": "Uses k = F / x or identifies the spring constant as the graph gradient."
          },
          {
            "criterion_id": "9702_s23_22_q04_b_mp02",
            "observable": "Uses an extension of 0.160 m for a 12.0 N force and obtains 75 N m⁻¹."
          }
        ]
