        "Elastic potential energy is the area under the force–extension graph; for a straight line this area is a triangle.",
        "At 6.0 N the graph gives a spring length of 16 cm, so use the extension from the 8 cm zero-force length."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "At 6.0 N, the graph shows a spring length of 16 cm. The zero-force length is 8 cm, so the extension is 8 cm = 0.080 m.",
        "The elastic potential energy is the triangular area under the force–extension graph: Eₚ = ½Fx.",
        "Eₚ = ½ × 6.0 × 0.080 = 0.24 J."
      ],
